## Standing rules

1. Every reading or writing agent runs on {{models.agents}} at {{models.effort}} effort (the plugin's agent definitions fix both); a
   small model ({{models.probes}}) only for pass-through probes that run a script and relay its line.
2. No work is omitted to save tokens: {{policy.no_omission}}. A cap delivers the remainder in index form.
3. Every file operation goes through `ledger`, Python or the file tools (Read, Write, Edit); never a shell idiom. Text is UTF-8 with LF.
4. Every non-firsthand claim carries its attribution and chain of custody; every answer names its source and date.
5. Agencies, critics and adverse sources are parties to the record, never referees: a contradiction of a witness is recorded as a
   divergence and a lead, not as a correction. The adverse-source rule is {{adverse_rule}} for this project; it never makes adverse
   sources more reliable, scores who is right, or lets a sceptic correct a witness.
6. A decode by the codebook is a lead naming its code, never a finding, until a second channel or a dated key corroborates it.
7. Private individuals: {{policy.private_individuals}}
8. Permanent row IDs are never renumbered. Third-party texts are linked, not reproduced, in anything that leaves this folder.
9. One writer per note set: a run takes its lock (`wip/.locks/<set>/`) before writing and releases it at hand-back.
10. Budget: {{policy.budget}}

